Found the issue! The Read function in the filesync provider **only checks if the local source file exists**, not if the remote file exists. Look at lines 425-432:

```go
if _, err := os.Stat(sourcePath); os.IsNotExist(err) {
    tflog.Info(ctx, "Source file no longer exists, removing resource from state", map[string]interface{}{
        "source": sourcePath,
    })
    // Source file was deleted - remove from state.
    resp.State.RemoveResource(ctx)
    return
}
```

It only checks `os.Stat(sourcePath)` - the **local** file. It doesn't SSH to the remote host to verify the destination file actually exists. That's why when we deleted `/config/static/traefik.yml` and ran `tofu plan`, it reported "No changes" - the local source file still existed, so the Read function was happy.

